WEBVTT

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:48.220
What is that? He's all wrapped up.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.600
That weapon is a flamethrower.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:51.850
Flame?

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:54.390
As in, that flame?

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:57.720
But that project should've been terminated a long time ago.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.940
And why was it terminated?

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.680
They realized...

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:08.460
...that it became a weapon that allowed humans to kill others in a way they shouldn't be.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.420
He's coming for us.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:12.690
It's cold...

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:19.770
It's cold...

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:25.120
So... I'm going to burn you guys...

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:36.150
It's cold...

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.380
So... I'm going to burn you guys...

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.280
All right!

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.610
Let's run by him like this!

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:41.700
Roger!

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.210
Burning people... warms up...

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:47.470
...my heart... a bit...

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.780
He scattered fuel over the water's surface?

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.680
It's like... a wall of flame, eh?

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:07.530
This guy's crazy...

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.330
Heck, doesn't he feel the heat?

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.470
Very well!

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.830
"You want to get through here, then defeat me."

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:28.580
That's what you're saying, right?

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.080
No, he didn't!

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:31.220
He didn't say anything!

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.460
Let go of me!

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.650
I won't have people say I ran away from a challenge!

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:37.360
There! There they are!!

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.800
Th-That's some crazy fire.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.300
You stood guard here to stop them?

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.680
Man, the boss sure likes to tease us.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.080
If he had a secret weapon like you, he should've told us first.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:55.130
Huh?

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:02.740
What? This guy's an enemy?!

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:03.850
Fire away!

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:14.330
Kill everyone...

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:16.790
Don't let anyone escape...

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.360
My orders...

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:25.640
Run!!!

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.200
Come on, get a grip!

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:37.170
Stop already!

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.580
You've killed enough, no?

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.580
That lantern...

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.020
901...

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:59.080
I'm from 908...

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.470
You're... my...

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:09.160
Corporal!

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:10.570
You mustn't hesitate!

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:13.080
He's not someone you can let your guard down against!

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.300
We're... on the same side...

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.340
901...

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.740
I'm not 901...

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:26.350
I'm part of...

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.570
What are they saying to each other?

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.060
What?!

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.300
What's going on?

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.230
This wasn't here just a moment ago!

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.860
O-Oreld!

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.700
After fire, we have to deal with water now?!

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.870
LT, this way's no good anymore!

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:01.210
Everyone, get out from there!

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:04.090
Corporal!

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:09.970
Corporal!

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:13.850
I'm part of...

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:17.650
I'm still...

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:34.460
You've finally awakened.

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:37.190
2nd Lieutenant...

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:40.060
What about the others?

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:41.210
They're all safe.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:42.450
Don't worry.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.090
I see.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.150
Hey, Corporal.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.030
What were you saying to that man?

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:03.790
Nothing, really.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:07.180
I see.

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:17.930
Anyway, focus on recuperating now.

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:19.810
Thank you, sir.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:22.910
Good bye, then.

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:24.270
Rest up well.

00:07:31.900 --> 00:07:34.720
Then, the people that wanted us dead were...

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:38.970
Without a doubt...

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:41.690
Our Himmel sales have decreased.

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:43.120
That's totally wrong!

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.380
They didn't have to do that to us!

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.770
Boss!

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:49.350
Leave everything to me.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:52.770
You guys just think about selling the drugs.

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:53.950
Damn it!

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.250
That's bullshit!

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:57.780
I have no choice...

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:01.230
...but to use these boys a bit more.

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:07.420
What's this?

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.720
Not a corpse, yet, eh?

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:14.340
You're Kauplan's assistant...

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.800
Now, I'm Kauplan.

00:08:21.070 --> 00:08:22.520
908?

00:08:23.280 --> 00:08:27.390
Ah, something like that did exist.

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:32.090
I developed the "protective fluid", so I remember them.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:33.730
Protective fluid?

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:38.050
There was a problem with the deployment of 908.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:40.570
No matter what kind of protective suit they wore,

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:44.540
they would always end up burning themselves due to the intense heat and flame.

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:48.150
That's where we thought of the protective fluid.

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:51.610
With its powerful insulation feature,

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:55.750
they can protect themselves from the fire by filling the suit with that fluid.

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:58.760
So that's what's inside that suit?

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:00.830
It's a lie.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:04.870
They were made to wear the suits by believing in that lie.

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:08.260
It's really just an anaesthetic used to dull your senses.

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:12.150
In other words, they can't really feel their own burns.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:16.350
Right now, I'm sure the skin under that suit is...

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:24.090
He doesn't even know what's happening to his own body...

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:26.010
...by using the flamethrower?

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:28.790
"Alt Schmied Jäger."

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:30.790
The one-eyed cremator.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:36.060
Alt Schmied was a one-eyed, one-legged deity of flame.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:39.010
Note: In Japanese folkore, "Ippon Datara" is a one-eyed, one-legged monster that lives in the mountains.
In Republic folklore, they called it a one-legged Datara.

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:41.520
He destroyed people with droughts,

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.160
and was the god that had forgotten about water and moisture.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:52.290
Will they really come?

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.940
I mean, given what happened just yesterday..

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:55.780
There's one.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:01.700
You are under arrest for a flagrant offense of selling Himmel.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.310
Released under bail.

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:07.990
After them!

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:09.300
Don't let them escape!

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:11.960
Secure the suspects and the evidence!

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:15.930
Secure them!

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:21.250
Would you guys just give up already?

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:24.070
Pumpkin or Pompkin or whatever...

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:26.580
What a stupid name, man!

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:28.560
I know about you guys.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:32.880
You guys are a joke inside the army, too.

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:35.240
What do you think you can do?

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:37.530
Here you go.

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.620
Oh, I need three packs of sugar, okay?

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:43.910
Give him three.

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:46.420
Released under bail.

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:49.540
Well then, if you'll excuse me.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:53.150
I feel bad now that you've made my coffee.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:55.060
I'll have it next time then.

00:10:55.060 --> 00:10:56.050
See ya.

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.580
Our section got this letter this morning.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:09.370
I think it's some sort of a warning.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:14.180
Did your secret investigation fail?

00:11:17.930 --> 00:11:20.240
Ralf... Smythson...

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:24.810
But why did they send it to Section III?

00:11:24.810 --> 00:11:28.900
It's not like civilians can tell the difference between Section I and Section III.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:34.470
Thanks, I guess.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:38.540
Aren't you hiding something from me?

00:11:38.540 --> 00:11:42.800
You guys at Section I are the highest organization in this country that handles public safety.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:46.250
You obviously know about the presence of Himmel there,

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:48.270
yet you're just sitting back and doing some nice secret investigation?

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.240
That's unlike you guys.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:53.670
I have no clue.

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:55.150
Excuse me.

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:58.130
Major Connelly!

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.260
...we couldn't...

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:11.000
...find the documents...

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:17.780
"We couldn't find the documents", eh?

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:19.920
What are they talking about?

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:24.160
We're going to have the bail revoked?

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:27.370
There's just no end to this arresting and releasing.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:29.640
I don't think this will work though.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:33.330
The LT's working too hard on this.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.560
Machs!

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:39.760
What is it?!

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:42.950
Marielle!

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:45.200
Don't scare me, man.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:48.120
It is you!

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.570
Ah...

00:12:50.570 --> 00:12:52.470
Do you remember me?

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:55.110
I saved you when those waterworks guys were trying to hit you

00:12:55.110 --> 00:12:59.260
and humbly left right after I asked your name... me, Sergeant Major Oreld!

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:01.880
Yes, I do.

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:04.410
You tried to touch me with your perverted eyes.

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:08.570
Man, I'm really...

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:11.140
Umm, it's okay.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:13.770
Oh, really?

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:16.280
You cut your hair, I see.

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:19.310
You're looking cuter than before.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:30.750
I'm so happy...

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:35.240
A man praised my looks...

00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:39.650
Does... does this hair really...

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:43.740
...not look strange?

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:51.390
It looks really nice.

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:16.140
Marielle... sorry...

00:14:18.130 --> 00:14:19.930
Here's my down payment.

00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:21.750
Take it.

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:24.230
The rest, I'll pay with a loan.

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:26.510
What's this about?

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.340
I'm buying your daughter.

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:33.050
You want the money to buy Himmel, right?!

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.490
Don't take me for an idiot!

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:38.070
What kind of parent would sell their children?!

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:39.650
It's too late for that, man.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:42.230
The girl's already sold her hair.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:45.580
She's sold part of her body already.

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:47.840
She did it for you, man!

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:50.920
Her body looks so delicious.

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:52.950
What's gotten into you, Oreld?

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.170
Please stop this!

00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:55.480
Oreld, you...

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:59.290
Now, let's go with a live strip-and-sex show!

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:02.160
No! Stop!

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:03.330
Quiet, you!

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:04.500
I already paid for you!

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.440
Shut up and strip!

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:07.510
Stop!!

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:12.740
Please stop!

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:21.480
This chick's pretty sexy!

00:15:22.110 --> 00:15:24.160
Let me have a part, too!

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.790
What kind of character are you?

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:29.320
Don't hold me responsible, man.

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:33.420
That was pushing it...

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:34.510
I give up.

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:37.170
Hey, hey, guys.

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:39.020
You guys think you can just watch this show for free?

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:42.400
I see, you guys don't have the money.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:44.770
You want to see the show, but you don't have the money.

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:47.220
You want the money but you don't work.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:49.710
Man, you people are such losers.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:53.690
Time for me to eat you up.

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:54.000
Watch how your daughter makes some money!

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:54.780
No!!!
Watch how your daughter makes some money!

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:54.800
Watch how your daughter makes some money!

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:57.020
Please stop!!!
Watch how your daughter makes some money!

00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:57.280
Please stop!!!

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:04.330
Don't touch my daughter!

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:10.290
Acting like a dad now?

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:13.900
Heck, by tomorrow, you'll be asking me for this deal.

00:16:13.900 --> 00:16:16.410
Losers will always be losers.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:17.740
Don't push yourselves too much.

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.100
Shut up!

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:21.320
What would you know?!

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:24.030
I lost everything...

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:28.090
I only have my daughter now!

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:35.320
Saying we're totally worthless...

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:37.550
We can work, too!

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:39.220
We can work,

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:41.380
whether it's tomorrow or right now!

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:43.350
We can work!

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:44.890
Right now!

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:49.250
I'll do anything for my daughter!

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:52.160
Even without Himmel!

00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:55.790
You listening, kid?!

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:58.620
You! You!

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:02.320
I can work whenever I want!

00:17:11.680 --> 00:17:14.180
Boss!

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:15.630
Boss?

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:21.610
Boss?

00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:36.020
Why's this guy...

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:44.270
And what's this?

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:45.870
They had a fight apparently.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:48.280
Oreld beat me.
Machs beat me.

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:48.290
Machs beat me.

00:17:50.080 --> 00:17:54.110
Umm, there's someone that wants to testify for our case.

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:54.940
What?!
Umm, there's someone that wants to testify for our case.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:54.960
Umm, there's someone that wants to testify for our case.

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:04.490
And, once every two weeks,

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:07.440
the boss gets everyone to leave the office.

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:12.410
The next morning, there will always be new goods distributed to everyone.

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:16.210
So, I think that's the day the transaction is done.

00:18:16.210 --> 00:18:17.160
LT!

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:21.400
If we nab him at the scene, we can prosecute Mione.

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:23.880
When's the next transaction day?

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:27.460
Metz.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:33.630
Probably... tonight...

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:41.770
I was just a street bum...

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:44.600
I had no job... no future...

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:47.550
I ate food I stole in the shadows of alleys...

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:50.980
My days were like that of a rat...

00:18:52.510 --> 00:18:56.100
But when I met the boss that day...

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:01.660
The boss took care of everything for someone like me.

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:05.830
But I knew it...

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:10.080
We're just being used.

00:19:10.680 --> 00:19:14.120
Bums will always be bums, right?

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:19.480
Even now, I'm selling and betraying my buddies...

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:20.760
...secretly informing you guys...

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:23.460
I'm just like a rat!

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:27.350
Rats can only be in the shadows...

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.670
...and just squeek all day, right?

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:33.850
You're wrong.

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:36.600
You're a pair of scissors.

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:37.610
Scissors?

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:38.870
Yes.

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:42.330
Using money, violence, and power,

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:49.900
Albert Mione is a war aggravator that protects himself within numerous layers of protection like a pumpkin.

00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:55.010
We fight every day to cut open those layers of protection.

00:19:56.400 --> 00:20:01.840
But, without a doubt, you were the one to cut open Mione's outer skin, Metz.

00:20:03.230 --> 00:20:05.340
You cannot underestimate the fangs of a rat.

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.810
Prepare for sortie immediately!

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:12.470
Time for another rumble, I guess.

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:13.290
Yes.

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:18.140
Hey, you're not going to arrest me?

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.830
We don't have time for you.

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:25.150
Sorry, but go surrender yourself to the police or something.

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:27.900
Are you okay, now?

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:28.640
Yes, sir.

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.830
She's messed up...

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:36.320
The fact that I might run away hasn't crossed her mind at all...

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.040
Damn it... I can't run away now...

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:44.640
Alice.

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:47.140
This isn't really a good time,

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:49.490
but let me borrow Oreld for a bit.

00:20:49.490 --> 00:20:51.270
I need to ask him to do something.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:52.060
Me?

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.950
You have an acquaintance in Section I, right?

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.130
A very personal one, that is.

00:20:57.660 --> 00:20:58.840
Yeah...

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:01.780
Ready, sir.

00:21:03.270 --> 00:21:04.320
That's?

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.360
Tonight, we settle this once and for all.

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:10.280
2nd Lieutenant!

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:13.380
If that guy shows up...

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:15.300
Can you let me handle him?

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:17.710
I beg of you!

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:20.540
No.

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:24.960
You're hiding something from me.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.170
B-But... Lieutenant!

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:28.110
No.

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:29.300
I'm fighting.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:32.590
Pumpkin Scissors, roll out!

00:21:32.590 --> 00:21:33.620
Roger that!

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:46.940
We've been waiting for you.

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:56.080
We are all servants of the Silver Wheel.

00:23:31.020 --> 00:23:34.060
Mer-kun, there's a huge development in the waterworks case!

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:35.680
Alice vs. Claymore-One!

00:23:35.680 --> 00:23:38.140
Behold, the slash of the double-edged sword, Mähne.

00:23:38.780 --> 00:23:40.930
Next time, "The Slasher".

00:23:40.930 --> 00:23:43.180
Come get us if you're not scared!!
